      "content": {
        "text": "Skip to main content\nCurrent language:\nEnglish\nClick to select different language\nPress centre\nDonate\nWhat we do\nResearch and reports\nStories\nWho we are\nTake action\nUNICEF\nHumanitarian appeal 2026\nUNICEF calls for urgent investment as humanitarian needs reach new extremes\nLearn more\nUNICEF, for every child\nRemarks\n27 March 2026\nAn average of 19,000 children displaced daily as escalating violence uproots 20 per cent of Lebanon's population in three weeks\nRead now\nPress release\n26 March 2026\nUNICEF Chief calls for urgent global support as children in Somalia face worsening malnutrition\nRead now\nExplainer\nHow to talk to your children about conflict and war\n8 tips to support and comfort your children\nGo to UNICEF Parenting\nAppeal\nChildren in Gaza need life-saving support\nUNICEF continues to work with partners to provide assistance to children and their families\nRead now\nAppeal\nEmergency response in Sudan\nOngoing conflict is pushing already vulnerable children deeper into hardship\nRead now\nExplainer\nProtecting children on the move\nWhat you need to know about the numbers, causes and rights of children affected by migration and displacement.\nRead now\nStatement\n10 December 2025\nAge restrictions alone won't keep children safe online\nRead now\nArticle\nOne year after the earthquake\nWhy child-friendly spaces still matter for children in Myanmar.\nGo to UNICEF Myanmar\nUNICEF\u2019s work\nUNICEF works in over 190 countries and territories to save children's lives, to defend their rights, and to help them fulfil their potential, from early childhood through adolescence. And we never give up.\nDiscover UNICEF's work for every child, everywhere.\nExplore what we do\nSpotlight\nGet inspired, get involved. Explore key UNICEF campaigns and initiatives.\nPage\nConvention on the Rights of the Child\nFind out about the world\u2019s most widely ratified human rights treaty in history\nVisit the page\nPartner site\nUNICEF Parenting\nBringing together some of the world\u2019s leading baby experts to help parents give their children the best start in life\nLearn more\nPartner site\nU-Report\nA community for young people, by young people, where they can raise their voices and share opinions on topics that matter to them.\nLearn more\nPage\nSustainable Development Goals\nAre we on track to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals for children?\nVisit the page\nSubscribe to UNICEF's newsletter\nA monthly digest that broadens your outlook, with children\u2019s rights kept in focus.\nSign up\nUNICEF home\nWhat we do\nResearch and reports\nStories and features\nWhere we work\nPress centre\nTake action\nAbout us\nWork with us\nPartner with UNICEF\nUNICEF Executive Board\nEvaluation\nEthics\nInternal Audit and Investigations\nTransparency and accountability\nSafeguarding\nSustainable Development Goals\nFrequently asked questions (FAQ)\nRelated UNICEF sites\nUNICEF Data\nUNICEF Parenting\nU-Report, for youth\nGlobal Shared Services Centre\nUNICEF Digital Impact\nSupport UNICEF\n\u042e\u041d\u0418\u0421\u0415\u0424 \u043d\u0430 \u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u043e\u043c\nBecome a donor\nVisit us on Facebook\nVisit us on Twitter\nVisit us on Instagram\nVisit us on YouTube\nVisit us on LinkedIn\nVisit us on WhatsApp\nContact us\nLegal\nReport fraud, abuse, wrongdoing\nAccessibility\nCookie settings\nUNICEF strives to uphold the rights of every child, protecting them from harm and all forms of discrimination, so that they can grow up healthy and educated to reach their full potential. This work is in line with UNICEF\u2019s globally recognized mandate and its support of national priorities.\nAbout cookies on UNICEF.org\nWe use cookies to enhance your experience, analyze site performance, and deliver personalized content and ads. You can accept all cookies, reject non-essential cookies, or customize your preferences. For more information, see our Cookie Policy & Privacy Policy.\nAccept all\nReject all\nCustomize",
